## Verdict
FAIL on criterion (e): the new "same at the start" branch introduced by
this task can render two different dollar figures while asserting they are
equal, reproduced against the real production code with a realistic
monthly-living-expense value (not an extreme/synthetic magnitude). This is
squarely in scope — the new `else` branch is this task's own addition, and
the failure mode is the literal one criterion (e) was written to rule out.

Recommended fix (for the record, not prescriptive): compute `base`/`start`
as rounded cents once (e.g. `math.Round(v*100)/100`) and drive BOTH the
differ/same comparison and the two `FormatMoney` calls from the same
rounded value, so there is one rounding computation, not two.
